THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the copy constructor doesn’t guarantee non-null initialization of `texture` on all paths. The constructor only calls `setRegion(region)`, and that method takes `@Nullable TextureRegion region` and dereferences it without a null check. NullAway likely assumes `region` could be null or that an exception in `setRegion` might prevent `texture` from being set. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I can add an explicit null check in the copy constructor (throwing an IllegalArgumentException like other constructors) and directly assign `this.texture = region.texture` before calling `setRegion(region)`. This ensures `texture` is definitely assigned in the constructor body on all non-exceptional paths. I’ll edit the file accordingly using sed.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '71,73c\  /** Constructs a region with the same texture and coordinates of the specified region. */
  public TextureRegion(TextureRegion region) {
    if (region == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("region cannot be null.");
    this.texture = region.texture;
    setRegion(region);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/TextureRegion.java
```

